@startuml
title What an `api` layer would and would not absorb\n(measured on the working tree: 43 distinct names cross into config+engine)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<proposed>> #E8F0FE
  BorderColor<<proposed>> #1A73E8
}

rectangle "tooling\n21 of 33 modules reach down" as TOOL
rectangle "runtime\nhook, log_writer, session_start" as RT
rectangle "api  (proposed)\ndecide(), RuntimeVerdict" <<proposed>> as API
rectangle "engine  -- 11 of the 43 names\nresolve (8), compound (3)\npermission_resolution: consumed by NOBODY" as ENG
rectangle "config  -- 32 of the 43 names\nconfig (10), rule_sort (7), rule_entry (5),\npermission_migration (4), config_write_guard (3), ..." as CFG

TOOL -[#1A73E8,bold]-> API
RT   -[#1A73E8,bold]-> API
API  -[#1A73E8,bold]-> ENG

TOOL -[#B31412,dashed]-> CFG
RT   -[#B31412,dashed]-> CFG
ENG  --> CFG

legend bottom
  <b>blue</b>  what an api layer sited above `engine` can absorb: 11 names (26%)
  <b><color:#B31412>red</color></b>  what it cannot, because the target is BELOW it: 32 names (74%)
  R6 is titled "the ENGINE has a public interface". Three quarters of the
  actual crossing surface is config-layer, not engine-layer.
end legend
@enduml
